  'Logistics and Transportation Management',
  'Logistics and Transportation Management',
  'Logistics and Transportation Management prepares students to move goods through complex supply networks with discipline, speed, reliability, cost awareness, regulatory fluency, and resilience. Students study modal choice, carrier management, freight pricing, routing, distribution networks, warehousing interfaces, last-mile delivery, international logistics, customs compliance, transportation technology, analytics, sustainability, and disruption response. The course culminates in a professional transportation case in which students recommend and defend an executable logistics network decision.',
  $ltmjson${"slug": "logistics-and-transportation-management", "title": "Logistics and Transportation Management", "description": "Logistics and Transportation Management prepares students to move goods through complex supply networks with discipline, speed, reliability, cost awareness, regulatory fluency, and resilience. Students study modal choice, carrier management, freight pricing, routing, distribution networks, warehousing interfaces, last-mile delivery, international logistics, customs compliance, transportation technology, analytics, sustainability, and disruption response. The course culminates in a professional transportation case in which students recommend and defend an executable logistics network decision.", "topics": [{"id": "adec1308-9455-4ea4-9c7f-895b08b42bcb", "type": "topic", "title": "Logistics Strategy and Supply Chain Role", "description": "This unit frames logistics as the system that converts supply-chain strategy into reliable flow, service, cost control, and resilience.", "children": [{"id": "7b8a3310-001d-4cd0-8d4d-d3ea52447114", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logistics Value Proposition", "children": [{"id": "503834fb-f029-4131-914b-2f433d32e952", "type": "concept", "title": "Place and time utility"}, {"id": "62a8cf13-1633-4cde-abc7-5f4dd41636c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Service level, cost, speed, reliability, and flexibility trade-offs"}, {"id": "f7d9750f-5981-4274-ac4a-cf974f2f53ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Logistics role in omnichannel, manufacturing, retail, and global supply chains"}], "description": "Students learn why logistics is not just shipping; it shapes service promises, customer experience, working capital, and competitive advantage."}, {"id": "4c9db9ac-29b5-43d8-944c-93d0edc1f350", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Total Cost and Service Thinking", "children": [{"id": "38701c65-f19a-4c28-867a-96796787d529", "type": "concept", "title": "Transportation, warehousing, inventory, packaging, handling, and stockout costs"}, {"id": "5be8532e-0b57-4288-8ec8-302b1c191175", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-to-serve and customer profitability"}, {"id": "509cf7b0-34ac-4bb7-9317-f896f6453777", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade-offs among freight speed, inventory buffer, and delivery promise"}], "description": "The point is to optimize the whole logistics system instead of minimizing one local cost."}, {"id": "607a325b-438a-412d-aa5b-4fa4522e85c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logistics Operating Models", "children": [{"id": "684ba51e-4e37-4c8e-9c1c-066c7a541500", "type": "concept", "title": "Centralized, decentralized, regional, and outsourced models"}, {"id": "ac5ccad3-46e8-4eff-b126-1a1d18480526", "type": "concept", "title": "3PL, 4PL, lead logistics provider, and asset-based carrier roles"}, {"id": "a4e50a7b-9054-4bed-b993-ffa2146a5e15", "type": "concept", "title": "Governance, accountability, and performance review cadence"}], "description": "Students compare the structures companies use to execute logistics across internal teams and partners."}]}, {"id": "0eee62c5-c17a-4c6f-9c7c-38737e12418e", "type": "topic", "title": "Transportation Modes and Modal Economics", "description": "This topic develops the core language of freight movement: what each mode does well, where it fails, and how modal economics shape network decisions.", "children": [{"id": "f2f2a5fd-c1c4-4eb1-a070-fd1ab6cfbb59", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mode Characteristics", "children": [{"id": "09239e9f-4ede-41d1-a780-8653c32501ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Speed, reliability, capacity, accessibility, damage risk, and cost"}, {"id": "d6d0cd7a-b8d6-40cb-9bdc-ca261f439f02", "type": "concept", "title": "Full truckload, less-than-truckload, parcel, railcar, container, air cargo, and bulk movement"}, {"id": "72705619-dbc8-4710-9a50-c92024cf1ae6", "type": "concept", "title": "Commodity, customer, lane, and urgency fit"}], "description": "Students learn how truck, rail, ocean, air, pipeline, parcel, and intermodal service differ."}, {"id": "88347ec4-8095-449d-9bfc-b3be76fa2cc9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modal Cost Drivers", "children": [{"id": "98692315-f252-4c0d-95ef-d68d78e9998f", "type": "concept", "title": "Linehaul, pickup and delivery, terminal handling, drayage, fuel, and accessorials"}, {"id": "d94c27a5-d17d-472b-a6d7-5da724eaccee", "type": "concept", "title": "Density, shipment size, load factor, and equipment utilization"}, {"id": "b2b230b5-7fab-457d-9ecb-ab02193e0dbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Backhaul imbalance and directional markets"}], "description": "The gist is that transportation cost is built from distance, weight, cube, equipment, labor, imbalance, fuel, and market capacity."}, {"id": "f6b3f896-d136-4e5a-9384-5424f7355dfc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modal Strategy", "children": [{"id": "46892469-e737-45b0-aa53-ca15af00fe66", "type": "concept", "title": "Mode shifts and intermodal conversion"}, {"id": "fd9ae732-1e36-495f-b7ab-52d2e8aa89d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Service promise versus freight spend"}, {"id": "5e2e8539-c543-4d6a-a92b-073c9cabc9e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Emissions, risk, resilience, and customer expectation implications"}], "description": "Students learn to choose modes based on total system performance rather than habit."}]}, {"id": "9a10bb57-5921-40d5-9eea-1f4ff4a3a795", "type": "topic", "title": "Carrier Selection, Procurement and Relationship Management", "description": "Carrier choices determine reliability, cost, risk, and customer service. This section teaches sourcing discipline and relationship management.", "children": [{"id": "4b5a405c-df50-4ba0-a1fc-0ec7e3491167", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Carrier Qualification", "children": [{"id": "41f11583-9da1-482e-8859-07d73f1eda83", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety record, insurance, authority, financial health, service footprint, and technology capability"}, {"id": "85276247-e62a-48fa-888e-4f8c8330f0e7", "type": "concept", "title": "On-time performance, claims ratio, tender acceptance, and responsiveness"}, {"id": "41a11822-adb4-4640-806d-f60e0c9ec586", "type": "concept", "title": "Diversity, sustainability, and strategic fit"}], "description": "Students learn how to evaluate carriers beyond price."}, {"id": "28bb5832-e9c2-4f6f-a762-886bc8678ca1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transportation Procurement", "children": [{"id": "02e5ed92-ebb9-4a57-ac4e-48ed47fc0704", "type": "concept", "title": "RFP design, lane data, bid sheets, service requirements, and award strategy"}, {"id": "4f11d4f6-878c-4d21-810f-7cb57bb51886", "type": "concept", "title": "Contract rates, spot rates, mini-bids, and dynamic procurement"}, {"id": "ca92156c-de5c-4e4c-a1f3-41a46e8e7270", "type": "concept", "title": "Negotiation, incumbent strategy, and carrier portfolio design"}], "description": "The point is to structure freight bids that produce usable capacity and fair comparisons."}, {"id": "93bac23b-f2c0-4f1e-8e72-f622f08580bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Carrier Performance Management", "children": [{"id": "19a13b46-83bb-40a9-b748-8d1185bfd94a", "type": "concept", "title": "Scorecards, QBRs, corrective action, escalation, and continuous improvement"}, {"id": "ff865b12-b3db-475b-b149-a94f563f4f17", "type": "concept", "title": "Tender acceptance, pickup/delivery performance, claims, billing accuracy, and communication"}, {"id": "a66e7543-00ec-459b-bb6c-fbd862c5e1ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Relationship segmentation: strategic, core, backup, and transactional carriers"}], "description": "Students learn how to govern transportation partners after award."}]}, {"id": "3baf4930-95a2-43f2-aca1-d3226036b7b6", "type": "topic", "title": "Freight Pricing, Contracts and Cost-to-Serve", "description": "This unit demystifies freight rates and teaches students how pricing, contracts, and cost allocation affect logistics decisions.", "children": [{"id": "11f48982-5f32-47af-9eea-3676b9d4fdc4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rate Structures", "children": [{"id": "dc3ca7da-312e-4d79-b6ae-26a9c8dd0164", "type": "concept", "title": "Tariffs, contract rates, spot quotes, mileage, weight breaks, dimensional weight, and class rates"}, {"id": "65b9203b-06d8-4892-8bb1-f59b7a4c278f", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessorials, detention, demurrage, fuel surcharge, and peak surcharges"}, {"id": "73ac9fb3-e1d0-4d60-8450-ea12c48c0f62", "type": "concept", "title": "Parcel zones, LTL classification, truckload lane rates, and ocean/air charges"}], "description": "Students learn common freight pricing formats and why the same shipment can produce different charges."}, {"id": "813e1892-69a9-4777-9fda-3c503d4a61e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contracts and Commercial Terms", "children": [{"id": "e2b2bb7c-1a92-42e0-8951-6a5c4d759bcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Service-level agreements, liability limits, payment terms, claims, and audit rights"}, {"id": "584ac79e-3c02-4806-a721-2a730f55db54", "type": "concept", "title": "Volume commitments, capacity commitments, rate validity, and index-linked fuel terms"}, {"id": "5ebccea7-2bb6-4435-9e3c-a7b61e0b287a", "type": "concept", "title": "Tender rules, cancellation, force majeure, and dispute resolution"}], "description": "The goal is to understand how transportation agreements allocate service expectations and risk."}, {"id": "35778713-db50-4780-ba0c-eebf63d4595c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cost-to-Serve Analysis", "children": [{"id": "d092e159-0150-49b1-ad88-89b0d6cf2ebe", "type": "concept", "title": "Activity-based costing for logistics"}, {"id": "84280ed9-0f65-42b5-b714-6ddec1ed2c7c", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer, SKU, order, and channel profitability"}, {"id": "b84f0ffe-8ca0-49f8-bb37-79dbd902a2be", "type": "concept", "title": "Freight audit, invoice matching, and leakage control"}], "description": "Students learn to connect freight cost to customers, products, lanes, and service policies."}]}, {"id": "bfb7b72b-ad04-4624-90f0-23c8e19eab9b", "type": "topic", "title": "Routing, Scheduling and Dispatch Optimization", "description": "Routing and scheduling convert customer promises into feasible transportation plans. Students learn both the logic and constraints behind vehicle movement.", "children": [{"id": "455e2ca2-74b4-479c-9557-e25177ce9899", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Routing Problems", "children": [{"id": "8a2fa151-ed77-490c-95c3-10e97d9e157a", "type": "concept", "title": "Vehicle routing problem, traveling salesperson problem, pickup and delivery, and backhaul matching"}, {"id": "7d396d98-2bdc-4e12-be0c-30c82f1b48de", "type": "concept", "title": "Distance, time windows, capacity, equipment, driver hours, and service constraints"}, {"id": "d237984f-50bd-407b-a877-6b0654eac111", "type": "concept", "title": "Manual planning versus optimization engines"}], "description": "Students learn the practical structure of routing decisions."}, {"id": "66b93daa-8d0e-45a3-ac82-ea030397124d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scheduling and Dispatch", "children": [{"id": "dccaea4f-10c5-41ab-b744-f3fb61edac5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Appointment scheduling, load sequencing, dock times, and dispatch boards"}, {"id": "55f1ade9-c238-4195-a563-aa891b83caae", "type": "concept", "title": "Driver assignment, equipment assignment, and route compliance"}, {"id": "4aa2c836-f4ac-401d-a9ea-0a80c1edd466", "type": "concept", "title": "Exception management, re-routing, and communication protocols"}], "description": "The focus is on execution: turning plans into timed work and responding to exceptions."}, {"id": "943a98cf-f191-4735-80ef-a37dfe6dda3e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Optimization Trade-offs", "children": [{"id": "fe1c6ef9-67fc-4a80-8631-383f71209e30", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, service, reliability, labor, safety, emissions, and customer priority"}, {"id": "3de8cd6d-b109-402c-be0d-6ac1c6b562b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitivity to demand variability and traffic"}, {"id": "70834844-8d7e-4b83-8ca1-2faa803f2bca", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario planning and what-if analysis"}], "description": "Students learn why the mathematically cheapest plan may not be operationally best."}]}, {"id": "8af4fa01-b9f4-47fe-8d81-4bd947dc24b9", "type": "topic", "title": "Distribution Network Design", "description": "A logistics network determines where inventory sits, how orders flow, and how fast customers can be served. This topic builds network design judgment.", "children": [{"id": "d353cf78-64b6-461e-97f1-7ca1fe497a82", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Network Structure", "children": [{"id": "54fe6c72-b9f1-42f7-96a2-6fb21fc0f28c", "type": "concept", "title": "Factories, suppliers, ports, DCs, cross-docks, stores, lockers, and customer nodes"}, {"id": "94c75ebe-5070-47af-9d94-a38fc773c9e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct shipping, hub-and-spoke, pooling, cross-docking, and postponement"}, {"id": "eaec3e22-5acc-485e-a5a9-0a3019aef6fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-echelon and multi-echelon networks"}], "description": "Students learn the design options that shape distribution systems."}, {"id": "2c1b40c1-a70a-4c32-8770-fd7ed1ea535c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Facility Location and Flow", "children": [{"id": "4aa5ec3f-f573-4b5e-aa80-2ea20a107b12", "type": "concept", "title": "Center-of-gravity, network optimization, and lane-flow modeling"}, {"id": "8af86266-b214-4cba-8e1f-b2973754b4d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Inbound, outbound, reverse, and transfer flows"}, {"id": "234a7b8d-fd39-461a-92cd-7b29724e5b04", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity, labor, real estate, tax, risk, and customer-density considerations"}], "description": "The point is to locate facilities and routes around demand, cost, capacity, and service."}, {"id": "e35b8c43-564a-4c48-8bce-ff87ab4a7ffd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Network Strategy", "children": [{"id": "c1a4775d-8af3-483f-866b-ea96f7a987cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Speed versus cost versus resilience"}, {"id": "f2430822-a741-4291-b785-48a7952b10d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Regionalization, nearshoring, and multi-sourcing"}, {"id": "fe45eaa2-4fb1-4d6e-94a5-9cf12ee8259d", "type": "concept", "title": "Network redesign triggers: growth, merger, disruption, service failure, and channel change"}], "description": "Students connect network design to business strategy."}]}, {"id": "3be74a70-643d-4611-99bd-006897d18d02", "type": "topic", "title": "Warehousing, Fulfillment and Inventory Interface", "description": "Transportation and warehousing are tightly linked: shipment size, order timing, storage design, and inventory policy all shape freight performance.", "children": [{"id": "85a07c05-150a-4411-b6fc-e8719875920e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Warehouse Role in Logistics", "children": [{"id": "5249b915-262c-46cd-831d-767a057f1fb7", "type": "concept", "title": "Receiving, putaway, storage, replenishment, picking, packing, shipping, and returns"}, {"id": "500882f6-4717-4007-b596-aca662101bee", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-docking, flow-through, breakbulk, and merge-in-transit"}, {"id": "90d3317b-ff59-44a7-83b2-9232d637505d", "type": "concept", "title": "Warehouse layout, slotting, labor, and dock management"}], "description": "Students learn how facilities support consolidation, postponement, fulfillment, and service."}, {"id": "fca38dea-36ea-47c6-a07c-383a545d82a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory-Service Trade-offs", "children": [{"id": "c81f1a02-a823-4855-8242-d14a4b5cd380", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle stock, safety stock, reorder points, EOQ, and ABC analysis"}, {"id": "2167e445-b98c-4af7-8d3c-5afa2b6b96b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Stockout risk, fill rate, order cycle time, and service levels"}, {"id": "ac4967d1-9cc9-4f88-a34b-fbfca5f17458", "type": "concept", "title": "Pooling, postponement, and inventory placement"}], "description": "The goal is to connect inventory policy to transportation speed and cost."}, {"id": "37dd844b-eb83-4bfd-bc74-21fc79bf954d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fulfillment Execution", "children": [{"id": "4be6a80b-30f8-400e-ab90-ec0d7829e37d", "type": "concept", "title": "Order batching, wave planning, picking methods, packing, labeling, and compliance"}, {"id": "cd835d4a-09d9-49db-a46f-26f02b114bd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Parcel, LTL, truckload, and customer pickup handoff"}, {"id": "ce044b97-7096-4c0f-b017-761679378017", "type": "concept", "title": "WMS, barcode, RFID, automation, and labor standards"}], "description": "Students learn the operational details behind customer-ready shipments."}]}, {"id": "479cdbd8-3b5e-4168-b4e7-c8662b11a207", "type": "topic", "title": "Demand Planning, S&OP and Capacity Alignment", "description": "Logistics cannot perform well when demand, inventory, and capacity plans are disconnected. This section links transportation decisions to planning cadence.", "children": [{"id": "cadbf517-f3a1-49e9-a210-b57815ca2acc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand Signals and Forecasts", "children": [{"id": "cefc0c3c-0ae2-4a69-abca-4a10b77de5d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand patterns, seasonality, promotions, launches, and forecast error"}, {"id": "ea77ad9f-0bf6-4d23-b1f3-285bd3e4d0cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Moving averages, exponential smoothing, causal forecasts, and judgment overlays"}, {"id": "2ba6028e-ce2b-4ac6-b50b-af0c6a3e22c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Forecast bias, accuracy, and exception review"}], "description": "Students learn what logistics planners need from demand planning."}, {"id": "17b9b079-1f94-4fb0-9194-85e0d2271d62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "S&OP and Logistics Capacity", "children": [{"id": "14e0c107-9347-40a3-ae86-53583719a62b", "type": "concept", "title": "Sales and operations planning cadence"}, {"id": "0fbcb30a-2349-4d02-a831-491690d3a5a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity planning for carriers, warehouses, ports, and labor"}, {"id": "71363be5-5b3d-4a53-93d7-8724b88e5a80", "type": "concept", "title": "Peak planning, constraint review, and contingency capacity"}], "description": "The purpose is to align freight capacity, warehouse labor, and inventory with expected demand."}, {"id": "fed4de7b-1d9f-471e-863d-983468564851", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integrated Planning Decisions", "children": [{"id": "26480dd3-97b8-4cef-b3e6-696c3af41a97", "type": "concept", "title": "Order frequency, minimum order quantities, replenishment cadence, and shipment consolidation"}, {"id": "cb4c1abc-fa7e-4d3a-9e09-13ce6476d323", "type": "concept", "title": "Expedite prevention and service policy design"}, {"id": "518e41c9-ebfd-4e5b-ac1d-115cf4f28650", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade-offs among forecast accuracy, buffer inventory, and transport flexibility"}], "description": "Students see how planning choices create logistics consequences."}]}, {"id": "1531c922-6ad0-4867-866f-a61f02cefad9", "type": "topic", "title": "Last-Mile, Ecommerce and Omnichannel Logistics", "description": "The last mile is often the most visible and expensive part of logistics. This topic focuses on customer promise, density, delivery options, and returns.", "children": [{"id": "2646c3b1-6dbe-4f9a-b98a-3e40578d1f97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Last-Mile Models", "children": [{"id": "78415b7e-5ee7-49f3-bda5-7e6efd318231", "type": "concept", "title": "Parcel networks, local courier, gig delivery, store fulfillment, lockers, pickup points, and white-glove service"}, {"id": "0d87b202-8415-4814-9bd8-c8859a1199ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Same-day, next-day, scheduled, and economy delivery options"}, {"id": "e457f9b1-1d9e-446f-b7bf-4b67dd70cc05", "type": "concept", "title": "Urban, suburban, and rural delivery economics"}], "description": "Students compare the delivery structures used in ecommerce and retail."}, {"id": "5f82851f-c6ef-4ef6-9905-6cd4ca470b1c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Customer Promise Design", "children": [{"id": "f3c18350-cd03-480d-824b-0f370ce20a90", "type": "concept", "title": "Delivery speed, accuracy, visibility, installation, returns, and communication"}, {"id": "825806d3-50c7-46b1-b110-23db1e81b406", "type": "concept", "title": "Free shipping thresholds, delivery fees, and service tiers"}, {"id": "13ccfb0c-4d69-4bfa-83a8-ed84146fd26e", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer experience metrics and failure recovery"}], "description": "The point is to design delivery promises that are attractive and operationally possible."}, {"id": "e8ec6480-369e-4c29-ba85-3f06bc71b975", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Returns and Reverse Flow", "children": [{"id": "0ecd41cd-548d-4c57-b445-8f0ee98ea58a", "type": "concept", "title": "Return authorization, inspection, disposition, refurbish, recycle, and resale"}, {"id": "ffe787ac-1759-444d-8c62-07249e963ff2", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost of returns and fraud control"}, {"id": "2fda9519-4deb-4702-8760-72ebe43a509d", "type": "concept", "title": "Reverse logistics network design and customer satisfaction"}], "description": "Students learn why returns are a strategic logistics process, not an afterthought."}]}, {"id": "9763ab87-a725-4497-bca2-9d634059907e", "type": "topic", "title": "International Logistics, Ports and Global Freight", "description": "Global logistics adds distance, time, uncertainty, regulation, and multi-party coordination. This unit introduces the operating logic of international freight.", "children": [{"id": "7916d05c-ddc3-410c-a535-d2cb0924d70c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global Freight Modes", "children": [{"id": "b9c7c6fb-4ffc-465e-a067-0307975cab71", "type": "concept", "title": "Containerization, vessels, ports, terminals, air cargo, rail corridors, and drayage"}, {"id": "4a200c09-1838-4140-8e43-910567cf0b07", "type": "concept", "title": "Transit time, cutoffs, sailings, dwell time, and port congestion"}, {"id": "57020432-36b5-49b1-833a-eedb5f187f70", "type": "concept", "title": "Freight forwarders, NVOCCs, brokers, and customs intermediaries"}], "description": "Students learn how ocean, air, rail, truck, and intermodal systems connect across borders."}, {"id": "e18aaef7-2871-443b-a028-9c04dab4f353", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Incoterms and Responsibilities", "children": [{"id": "86abd1d3-784c-442d-83d2-e06052b832be", "type": "concept", "title": "EXW, FCA, FOB, CFR, CIF, CPT, CIP, DAP, DPU, and DDP"}, {"id": "dacb274f-0b2a-4b59-b099-7d541c8ffcb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Transfer of risk, freight payment, insurance, and documentation responsibility"}, {"id": "38597835-dfd3-42aa-a20f-f58385b2267e", "type": "concept", "title": "Common incoterms mistakes and landed cost implications"}], "description": "The goal is to understand how commercial terms assign cost, risk, and responsibility."}, {"id": "a574abc0-6456-4bf9-aec6-d424ed851415", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global Risk and Coordination", "children": [{"id": "17695b3a-858d-4d0d-aaf7-b7ced4afc68c", "type": "concept", "title": "Geopolitical risk, port disruption, weather, labor actions, piracy, and sanctions"}, {"id": "c287f4ab-2466-479b-8796-ebac03b5101d", "type": "concept", "title": "Buffer time, alternate gateways, dual routing, and supplier coordination"}, {"id": "0e7841a6-e753-46e1-81bd-b82d11f74848", "type": "concept", "title": "Visibility, milestones, and exception management"}], "description": "Students learn how global logistics plans deal with uncertainty."}]}, {"id": "a308ad5d-bacf-447b-a07e-3e40121517db", "type": "topic", "title": "Customs, Trade Compliance and Security", "description": "Trade compliance protects the firm from delays, penalties, seizures, and reputational harm. Students learn the core compliance processes logistics managers must understand.", "children": [{"id": "25b50fd4-f5a0-4dee-8290-a692f91bc827", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Customs Documentation", "children": [{"id": "4d0f833b-2e12-40d2-8c97-c21cc37c5ee2", "type": "concept", "title": "Commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, airway bill, certificate of origin, and entry documents"}, {"id": "459a6b0a-42a1-40c6-a713-b9637b29d239", "type": "concept", "title": "HS classification, valuation, country of origin, and duty calculation"}, {"id": "1bb3a246-e27c-4b10-8187-c34b3de9fb8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Recordkeeping, audit trail, and broker coordination"}], "description": "Students learn the paperwork and data needed for legal cross-border movement."}, {"id": "abac3473-6c10-4d12-bf08-5cc3e1cdc459", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regulatory Compliance", "children": [{"id": "af37fddb-6b49-46f7-81fd-9ee5b5efa4f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Import/export controls, denied parties, sanctions, anti-dumping, and product regulations"}, {"id": "f98c82e3-7b73-46e1-9493-55f94f6c7cfa", "type": "concept", "title": "C-TPAT, bonded warehouses, free trade zones, and trusted trader programs"}, {"id": "b77a5aaa-6557-464a-b319-9944dabb8659", "type": "concept", "title": "Compliance ownership and escalation"}], "description": "The point is to connect logistics decisions to trade rules and government controls."}, {"id": "433fb844-4f94-4615-a939-9fe40cb32a02", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cargo Security and Risk", "children": [{"id": "20533039-8ab5-4463-9349-762d36b4ee30", "type": "concept", "title": "Chain of custody, seals, inspections, screening, and cargo theft prevention"}, {"id": "e47f0651-e596-4916-b8db-e5898af89c2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cybersecurity for logistics data and systems"}, {"id": "a94fce15-213b-4dc4-a4b6-af7d0729499d", "type": "concept", "title": "Insurance, claims, and incident response"}], "description": "Students learn how security requirements shape logistics execution."}]}, {"id": "5956e700-90f1-4df8-8a1b-c70f3307ecfc", "type": "topic", "title": "Intermodal, Multimodal and Infrastructure Systems", "description": "Modern logistics depends on infrastructure and handoffs across modes. This topic focuses on nodes, transfers, bottlenecks, and infrastructure capacity.", "children": [{"id": "464f0b9f-2224-4b9d-8c6b-5b547043e8c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intermodal Systems", "children": [{"id": "7c0e94b5-817c-4c85-88f4-123a8bc5e04c", "type": "concept", "title": "Drayage, ramps, terminals, chassis, containers, and rail intermodal"}, {"id": "f12c2fba-539f-43a6-bfd1-6371a1538320", "type": "concept", "title": "Ramp selection, cutoffs, dwell, detention, demurrage, and equipment availability"}, {"id": "456b2088-702e-4758-8f93-bb6c0ba8cd1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Intermodal cost, emissions, service, and reliability trade-offs"}], "description": "Students learn how containers and trailers move across truck, rail, ocean, and inland hubs."}, {"id": "3c567e4b-5728-46cc-8ecd-9aa709dd033f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Infrastructure and Bottlenecks", "children": [{"id": "87c5bbaa-ca74-4ad6-8895-86ae11a0db09", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity, congestion, maintenance, weather exposure, and labor availability"}, {"id": "c1528782-cdb2-44ad-be7e-c8825b92add3", "type": "concept", "title": "Port and terminal operations"}, {"id": "b277d586-b042-4740-8f97-8cc9e874ef70", "type": "concept", "title": "Public policy, infrastructure investment, and freight corridors"}], "description": "The focus is on how ports, roads, bridges, rail, airports, and warehouses constrain logistics performance."}, {"id": "eb57ccbb-72d0-400d-93ad-e0cb9a7ba6a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multimodal Coordination", "children": [{"id": "0780ab7a-285b-40cc-8b24-6ffbdedc6538", "type": "concept", "title": "Handoff milestones, documentation, visibility, and exception ownership"}, {"id": "34fceda4-8a10-42ec-bff4-21b63db901e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Through bills, freight forwarding, and integrated service providers"}, {"id": "b11853ed-3077-454c-b642-98beb6b54575", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk at interfaces and buffers between modes"}], "description": "Students learn how to manage movement when no single party controls the whole journey."}]}, {"id": "083b9dbc-21fe-4840-9559-224edc885408", "type": "topic", "title": "Logistics Technology, TMS, WMS and Visibility", "description": "Technology lets logistics teams plan, execute, monitor, and improve flow. This unit explains the systems landscape and how data becomes operational visibility.", "children": [{"id": "c63df780-71e6-4aed-ab18-9a7a4583c870", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transportation Management Systems", "children": [{"id": "e8f8f90f-a697-4692-8204-17204489aedd", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning, rating, tendering, tracking, freight audit, settlement, and reporting"}, {"id": "7fab82f2-1f9a-48b3-9b89-905b42322d77", "type": "concept", "title": "Carrier portals, EDI/API connectivity, and load boards"}, {"id": "7ccdf2cf-9f9f-4363-a871-270b3cd2442c", "type": "concept", "title": "Optimization, dynamic pricing, and exception workflows"}], "description": "Students learn what TMS platforms do and why they matter."}, {"id": "46fcdf62-3c4a-446b-a429-2d18a1d386ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Warehouse and Yard Systems", "children": [{"id": "c427d030-e000-4790-969e-d405f3fbfc03", "type": "concept", "title": "WMS, YMS, labor management, slotting, scanning, RFID, and automation"}, {"id": "a2450f82-cc23-4b52-9f0c-b2c70de4d3da", "type": "concept", "title": "Appointment scheduling, dock visibility, and trailer tracking"}, {"id": "43b8039f-ddba-4e54-bf75-60b022fe8f5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Integration among ERP, OMS, WMS, TMS, and carrier systems"}], "description": "The point is to understand how warehouse and yard execution systems connect to transport."}, {"id": "1aa520ae-0c78-4448-8fab-6bdd5e527500", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visibility and Control Towers", "children": [{"id": "8cbc4903-4f97-4806-9eb3-7497aa1b7eb3", "type": "concept", "title": "GPS, telematics, IoT sensors, ELDs, AIS, APIs, milestones, and event data"}, {"id": "0228e23a-d191-4ac4-b7cf-192a854e4780", "type": "concept", "title": "Predictive ETA, alerts, exception triage, and customer communication"}, {"id": "5acbba32-93e8-43fa-af94-825131580b70", "type": "concept", "title": "Data quality, master data, and governance"}], "description": "Students learn how real-time logistics data supports decision making."}]}, {"id": "fb514a10-fe2e-430f-80ad-cbb2e442b451", "type": "topic", "title": "Logistics Analytics, KPIs and Decision Support", "description": "World-class logistics managers use data to diagnose performance, evaluate trade-offs, and improve decisions. This section builds practical analytics fluency.", "children": [{"id": "37f6d923-184e-45b6-884b-735a9cc10dc9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logistics KPI Design", "children": [{"id": "a1c68186-2b0a-4961-ba44-7821379fd4a7", "type": "concept", "title": "On-time pickup, on-time delivery, tender acceptance, cost per mile, cost per order, claims, damage, dwell, and utilization"}, {"id": "5101b803-f5d8-4121-af01-adf7ab602af1", "type": "concept", "title": "Service, cost, productivity, quality, sustainability, and resilience metrics"}, {"id": "40eec463-0fa5-4afa-8b37-7dbd232755ca", "type": "concept", "title": "KPI definitions, targets, ownership, and review cadence"}], "description": "Students learn which measures matter and how to avoid metric overload."}, {"id": "7c3ccf72-c87c-461e-9104-ab1d5d1271b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Decision Analytics", "children": [{"id": "ead6b676-f486-4a65-a2e5-057cf5412686", "type": "concept", "title": "Lane analysis, shipment consolidation, mode choice, routing, and facility scenarios"}, {"id": "f0bb57df-ec58-4e5e-b742-44cc89729e65", "type": "concept", "title": "Regression, clustering, simulation, optimization, and dashboarding basics"}, {"id": "44259d9a-909d-42ac-8ba1-e6fd8975374b", "type": "concept", "title": "Data visualization and executive decision briefs"}], "description": "The goal is to model logistics choices using clear assumptions and sensitivity."}, {"id": "ea1d47c0-0c42-4265-93e1-ae1d43e3e061", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Performance Improvement", "children": [{"id": "fd9451a5-66dc-4b22-bd07-af3cc34fe3b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Root-cause analysis, Pareto analysis, control charts, and variance review"}, {"id": "88951349-c243-41aa-aeb4-3c24897fa135", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuous improvement projects and benefits tracking"}, {"id": "5299e796-d7bf-42de-9d81-7ba765dec970", "type": "concept", "title": "Benchmarking against internal history and external data"}], "description": "Students learn to turn metrics into action."}]}, {"id": "96a426f3-a2d5-4921-ae5f-defcfcbe54e1", "type": "topic", "title": "Risk, Resilience and Disruption Response", "description": "Logistics networks operate under disruption. This topic teaches students to map risk, prepare contingencies, and recover service.", "children": [{"id": "5ffff245-5218-4e33-b4dc-e07b8ff44114", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Risk Identification", "children": [{"id": "c9be27fa-0b9d-463c-8faa-30967af145e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier, carrier, lane, port, facility, weather, cyber, labor, geopolitical, and demand risks"}, {"id": "33b7ef82-8db3-40d0-9057-73b5909a1332", "type": "concept", "title": "Single points of failure and critical nodes"}, {"id": "70d541bf-0911-437e-bde7-a12965768ecf", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk probability, impact, detectability, and velocity"}], "description": "Students learn to recognize vulnerabilities before they become crises."}, {"id": "b19a50b6-ab7b-4a78-8ffc-02652eaaf7a3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resilience Design", "children": [{"id": "99210d28-14ec-4f64-83cc-8fa7e2511ed2", "type": "concept", "title": "Redundant carriers, alternate ports, safety capacity, inventory buffers, and flexible routing"}, {"id": "8ef84776-68b4-4b99-8361-22ab06da036c", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario planning, playbooks, and business continuity planning"}, {"id": "78e57d5e-9dd5-4a0e-8040-9d29cc1796fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade-offs among efficiency, resilience, and working capital"}], "description": "The point is to build optionality without making the network unaffordable."}, {"id": "de59c4b0-3e58-4d96-a0d5-3ce746050eda", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Disruption Response", "children": [{"id": "790759ef-6ae0-4d17-b06d-ca1cac4a4555", "type": "concept", "title": "War rooms, escalation, decision rights, communications, and recovery priorities"}, {"id": "e9a4d297-e900-4a7b-91aa-5ffd4c627ff8", "type": "concept", "title": "Expediting, allocation, substitution, and customer segmentation during disruption"}, {"id": "56ee1fe4-a7e4-4900-9b80-33693cea9f05", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-event learning and resilience investment cases"}], "description": "Students learn the operating discipline of crisis logistics."}]}, {"id": "ddcc295a-6538-44da-8cf8-99f443ac7be2", "type": "topic", "title": "Sustainable and Responsible Logistics", "description": "Logistics choices affect emissions, communities, labor, safety, and waste. This section makes sustainability an operational design problem.", "children": [{"id": "bc1a7a4e-99f8-45c0-bc91-7b00be61c46e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Emissions and Energy", "children": [{"id": "dd0701dc-e368-4dc6-a537-593bb7b96a3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope 1, Scope 2, and Scope 3 logistics emissions"}, {"id": "fa4e2ce1-7764-44fc-987d-b3babd8134a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Mode shift, route optimization, load factor, alternative fuels, EVs, and renewable energy"}, {"id": "34891231-709f-4e2e-b32f-4858d8431f15", "type": "concept", "title": "Carbon accounting, emissions factors, and customer reporting"}], "description": "Students learn where logistics emissions come from and how to reduce them."}, {"id": "7bfc2211-78b7-4478-8116-6b6c2a4a3159", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Circular and Reverse Logistics", "children": [{"id": "62667990-5896-4047-9213-5bc60696c04d", "type": "concept", "title": "Returns, repair, refurbishment, remanufacturing, recycling, and disposal"}, {"id": "457f4b5c-0b23-42be-9273-0589e4014d1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Packaging reduction, reusable packaging, and closed-loop systems"}, {"id": "87993a00-26fd-405c-95b3-50a28be820d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Product design and logistics design for circularity"}], "description": "The focus is on recovering value and reducing waste."}, {"id": "64787e5a-cd29-4327-9f04-aaffcad558ce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social Responsibility", "children": [{"id": "9848f928-e98e-42fa-a3c6-062f1463a4e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Driver safety, labor practices, warehouse ergonomics, and fair scheduling"}, {"id": "d1aa1e8c-c99e-4e6c-810b-0362e19f5ff6", "type": "concept", "title": "Community impacts of freight, congestion, noise, and air quality"}, {"id": "c4cb41a0-9ead-458e-9468-9283ecd95a3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical sourcing, transparency, and supplier/carrier standards"}], "description": "Students learn that responsible logistics includes people and communities."}]}, {"id": "4f8d0c5f-c3b0-4413-b6af-32dfdd987fbf", "type": "topic", "title": "Regulation, Safety and Legal Environment", "description": "Transportation operates in a regulated environment. Students learn the rules and responsibilities that shape safe, lawful logistics execution.", "children": [{"id": "6fde868b-b4f8-4124-a3f7-f9d14e6fbd7a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transportation Regulation", "children": [{"id": "b97fbfd6-e96b-41fd-9176-a5243c7e990f", "type": "concept", "title": "Motor carrier authority, hours of service, ELDs, hazardous materials, and safety ratings"}, {"id": "54c23b8f-9613-42b0-a16e-c164fccfd969", "type": "concept", "title": "Rail, ocean, air, and parcel regulatory context"}, {"id": "76298ab3-17ed-4812-a61c-b86c87c639d3", "type": "concept", "title": "FMCSA, DOT, FMC, FAA, TSA, and international bodies"}], "description": "Students learn the regulatory basics that differ by mode and jurisdiction."}, {"id": "fbe05152-227d-429e-97b2-fa949c9ca480", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Safety Management", "children": [{"id": "7adda5bf-5534-45b3-a253-ad813fe1f18a", "type": "concept", "title": "Driver safety, warehouse safety, loading securement, hazmat handling, and incident reporting"}, {"id": "4dc7f6dc-2247-4406-bbaa-3d596186f548", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety KPIs, audits, training, and corrective actions"}, {"id": "29c1f42e-05f0-403c-a8ff-c54c10ce4e32", "type": "concept", "title": "Insurance, liability, claims, and risk transfer"}], "description": "The goal is to make safety a managed system, not a slogan."}, {"id": "969bb369-8b4d-4b35-b0fb-4b6b7f39557c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Legal and Ethical Issues", "children": [{"id": "7d741b3e-600c-4729-a757-0b44aad59bda", "type": "concept", "title": "Contracts, fraud, cargo theft, bribery, sanctions, antitrust, and confidentiality"}, {"id": "cf400d92-4514-4568-88ff-3490c9dff54f", "type": "concept", "title": "Data privacy and cybersecurity in logistics platforms"}, {"id": "d8e6ac3c-91ff-4e98-8dd6-f797fce85cdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical decision making under service and cost pressure"}], "description": "Students learn common legal and ethical pitfalls in logistics."}]}, {"id": "ad8c3115-23e2-4470-a89a-de1a9852b783", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone Transportation Case and Network Recommendation", "description": "The course culminates in a professional logistics decision case. Students diagnose a network, model alternatives, and recommend an executable transportation plan.", "children": [{"id": "d0f9096c-bf97-4b5b-9791-29bd442880b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case Diagnosis", "children": [{"id": "72d21274-9d67-45e7-81be-477a5ab57dd2", "type": "concept", "title": "Current network, lanes, modes, volumes, costs, service failures, and constraints"}, {"id": "23225530-ddd4-44de-ba18-fad018b7f9ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholders, customer promise, inventory impact, and risk exposure"}, {"id": "07c6d046-4df6-4816-8a10-4fa10c3ab298", "type": "concept", "title": "Data gaps, assumptions, and decision criteria"}], "description": "Students begin by defining the logistics problem and its business stakes."}, {"id": "d1d090ba-bb2a-4426-9653-f9efbaf8c966", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Alternative Design", "children": [{"id": "0476591b-923c-4b26-864f-2725c528aafb", "type": "concept", "title": "Mode mix, carrier strategy, routing, facility use, last-mile design, and technology support"}, {"id": "c64386cc-f1f6-465a-bcf1-f62de6969535", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, service, emissions, resilience, and implementation trade-offs"}, {"id": "eb8782c3-9822-478b-8c2a-15cf237f7ff8", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitivity analysis and scenario planning"}], "description": "The capstone requires students to create and compare feasible logistics options."}, {"id": "ff97c125-948a-42cd-8d97-de98c61558fe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Executive Recommendation", "children": [{"id": "57d5b704-16cd-4b6e-b292-7b6a9f45c209", "type": "concept", "title": "Recommendation memo, dashboard, network map, and implementation roadmap"}, {"id": "69554be6-8c78-4287-b621-665fd951e981", "type": "concept", "title": "Carrier, warehouse, systems, compliance, and change-management actions"}, {"id": "323789a3-2572-43ba-abed-a73246c7be9a", "type": "concept", "title": "KPIs, control plan, and post-implementation review"}], "description": "Students finish by presenting a decision-ready logistics plan."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$ltmjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'logistics-and-transportation-management'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Logistics and Transportation Management',
  goal = 'Logistics and Transportation Management',
  summary = 'Logistics and Transportation Management prepares students to move goods through complex supply networks with discipline, speed, reliability, cost awareness, regulatory fluency, and resilience. Students study modal choice, carrier management, freight pricing, routing, distribution networks, warehousing interfaces, last-mile delivery, international logistics, customs compliance, transportation technology, analytics, sustainability, and disruption response. The course culminates in a professional transportation case in which students recommend and defend an executable logistics network decision.',
  data = $ltmjson${"slug": "logistics-and-transportation-management", "title": "Logistics and Transportation Management", "description": "Logistics and Transportation Management prepares students to move goods through complex supply networks with discipline, speed, reliability, cost awareness, regulatory fluency, and resilience. Students study modal choice, carrier management, freight pricing, routing, distribution networks, warehousing interfaces, last-mile delivery, international logistics, customs compliance, transportation technology, analytics, sustainability, and disruption response. The course culminates in a professional transportation case in which students recommend and defend an executable logistics network decision.", "topics": [{"id": "adec1308-9455-4ea4-9c7f-895b08b42bcb", "type": "topic", "title": "Logistics Strategy and Supply Chain Role", "description": "This unit frames logistics as the system that converts supply-chain strategy into reliable flow, service, cost control, and resilience.", "children": [{"id": "7b8a3310-001d-4cd0-8d4d-d3ea52447114", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logistics Value Proposition", "children": [{"id": "503834fb-f029-4131-914b-2f433d32e952", "type": "concept", "title": "Place and time utility"}, {"id": "62a8cf13-1633-4cde-abc7-5f4dd41636c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Service level, cost, speed, reliability, and flexibility trade-offs"}, {"id": "f7d9750f-5981-4274-ac4a-cf974f2f53ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Logistics role in omnichannel, manufacturing, retail, and global supply chains"}], "description": "Students learn why logistics is not just shipping; it shapes service promises, customer experience, working capital, and competitive advantage."}, {"id": "4c9db9ac-29b5-43d8-944c-93d0edc1f350", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Total Cost and Service Thinking", "children": [{"id": "38701c65-f19a-4c28-867a-96796787d529", "type": "concept", "title": "Transportation, warehousing, inventory, packaging, handling, and stockout costs"}, {"id": "5be8532e-0b57-4288-8ec8-302b1c191175", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost-to-serve and customer profitability"}, {"id": "509cf7b0-34ac-4bb7-9317-f896f6453777", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade-offs among freight speed, inventory buffer, and delivery promise"}], "description": "The point is to optimize the whole logistics system instead of minimizing one local cost."}, {"id": "607a325b-438a-412d-aa5b-4fa4522e85c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logistics Operating Models", "children": [{"id": "684ba51e-4e37-4c8e-9c1c-066c7a541500", "type": "concept", "title": "Centralized, decentralized, regional, and outsourced models"}, {"id": "ac5ccad3-46e8-4eff-b126-1a1d18480526", "type": "concept", "title": "3PL, 4PL, lead logistics provider, and asset-based carrier roles"}, {"id": "a4e50a7b-9054-4bed-b993-ffa2146a5e15", "type": "concept", "title": "Governance, accountability, and performance review cadence"}], "description": "Students compare the structures companies use to execute logistics across internal teams and partners."}]}, {"id": "0eee62c5-c17a-4c6f-9c7c-38737e12418e", "type": "topic", "title": "Transportation Modes and Modal Economics", "description": "This topic develops the core language of freight movement: what each mode does well, where it fails, and how modal economics shape network decisions.", "children": [{"id": "f2f2a5fd-c1c4-4eb1-a070-fd1ab6cfbb59", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mode Characteristics", "children": [{"id": "09239e9f-4ede-41d1-a780-8653c32501ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Speed, reliability, capacity, accessibility, damage risk, and cost"}, {"id": "d6d0cd7a-b8d6-40cb-9bdc-ca261f439f02", "type": "concept", "title": "Full truckload, less-than-truckload, parcel, railcar, container, air cargo, and bulk movement"}, {"id": "72705619-dbc8-4710-9a50-c92024cf1ae6", "type": "concept", "title": "Commodity, customer, lane, and urgency fit"}], "description": "Students learn how truck, rail, ocean, air, pipeline, parcel, and intermodal service differ."}, {"id": "88347ec4-8095-449d-9bfc-b3be76fa2cc9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modal Cost Drivers", "children": [{"id": "98692315-f252-4c0d-95ef-d68d78e9998f", "type": "concept", "title": "Linehaul, pickup and delivery, terminal handling, drayage, fuel, and accessorials"}, {"id": "d94c27a5-d17d-472b-a6d7-5da724eaccee", "type": "concept", "title": "Density, shipment size, load factor, and equipment utilization"}, {"id": "b2b230b5-7fab-457d-9ecb-ab02193e0dbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Backhaul imbalance and directional markets"}], "description": "The gist is that transportation cost is built from distance, weight, cube, equipment, labor, imbalance, fuel, and market capacity."}, {"id": "f6b3f896-d136-4e5a-9384-5424f7355dfc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modal Strategy", "children": [{"id": "46892469-e737-45b0-aa53-ca15af00fe66", "type": "concept", "title": "Mode shifts and intermodal conversion"}, {"id": "fd9ae732-1e36-495f-b7ab-52d2e8aa89d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Service promise versus freight spend"}, {"id": "5e2e8539-c543-4d6a-a92b-073c9cabc9e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Emissions, risk, resilience, and customer expectation implications"}], "description": "Students learn to choose modes based on total system performance rather than habit."}]}, {"id": "9a10bb57-5921-40d5-9eea-1f4ff4a3a795", "type": "topic", "title": "Carrier Selection, Procurement and Relationship Management", "description": "Carrier choices determine reliability, cost, risk, and customer service. This section teaches sourcing discipline and relationship management.", "children": [{"id": "4b5a405c-df50-4ba0-a1fc-0ec7e3491167", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Carrier Qualification", "children": [{"id": "41f11583-9da1-482e-8859-07d73f1eda83", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety record, insurance, authority, financial health, service footprint, and technology capability"}, {"id": "85276247-e62a-48fa-888e-4f8c8330f0e7", "type": "concept", "title": "On-time performance, claims ratio, tender acceptance, and responsiveness"}, {"id": "41a11822-adb4-4640-806d-f60e0c9ec586", "type": "concept", "title": "Diversity, sustainability, and strategic fit"}], "description": "Students learn how to evaluate carriers beyond price."}, {"id": "28bb5832-e9c2-4f6f-a762-886bc8678ca1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transportation Procurement", "children": [{"id": "02e5ed92-ebb9-4a57-ac4e-48ed47fc0704", "type": "concept", "title": "RFP design, lane data, bid sheets, service requirements, and award strategy"}, {"id": "4f11d4f6-878c-4d21-810f-7cb57bb51886", "type": "concept", "title": "Contract rates, spot rates, mini-bids, and dynamic procurement"}, {"id": "ca92156c-de5c-4e4c-a1f3-41a46e8e7270", "type": "concept", "title": "Negotiation, incumbent strategy, and carrier portfolio design"}], "description": "The point is to structure freight bids that produce usable capacity and fair comparisons."}, {"id": "93bac23b-f2c0-4f1e-8e72-f622f08580bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Carrier Performance Management", "children": [{"id": "19a13b46-83bb-40a9-b748-8d1185bfd94a", "type": "concept", "title": "Scorecards, QBRs, corrective action, escalation, and continuous improvement"}, {"id": "ff865b12-b3db-475b-b149-a94f563f4f17", "type": "concept", "title": "Tender acceptance, pickup/delivery performance, claims, billing accuracy, and communication"}, {"id": "a66e7543-00ec-459b-bb6c-fbd862c5e1ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Relationship segmentation: strategic, core, backup, and transactional carriers"}], "description": "Students learn how to govern transportation partners after award."}]}, {"id": "3baf4930-95a2-43f2-aca1-d3226036b7b6", "type": "topic", "title": "Freight Pricing, Contracts and Cost-to-Serve", "description": "This unit demystifies freight rates and teaches students how pricing, contracts, and cost allocation affect logistics decisions.", "children": [{"id": "11f48982-5f32-47af-9eea-3676b9d4fdc4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rate Structures", "children": [{"id": "dc3ca7da-312e-4d79-b6ae-26a9c8dd0164", "type": "concept", "title": "Tariffs, contract rates, spot quotes, mileage, weight breaks, dimensional weight, and class rates"}, {"id": "65b9203b-06d8-4892-8bb1-f59b7a4c278f", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessorials, detention, demurrage, fuel surcharge, and peak surcharges"}, {"id": "73ac9fb3-e1d0-4d60-8450-ea12c48c0f62", "type": "concept", "title": "Parcel zones, LTL classification, truckload lane rates, and ocean/air charges"}], "description": "Students learn common freight pricing formats and why the same shipment can produce different charges."}, {"id": "813e1892-69a9-4777-9fda-3c503d4a61e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contracts and Commercial Terms", "children": [{"id": "e2b2bb7c-1a92-42e0-8951-6a5c4d759bcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Service-level agreements, liability limits, payment terms, claims, and audit rights"}, {"id": "584ac79e-3c02-4806-a721-2a730f55db54", "type": "concept", "title": "Volume commitments, capacity commitments, rate validity, and index-linked fuel terms"}, {"id": "5ebccea7-2bb6-4435-9e3c-a7b61e0b287a", "type": "concept", "title": "Tender rules, cancellation, force majeure, and dispute resolution"}], "description": "The goal is to understand how transportation agreements allocate service expectations and risk."}, {"id": "35778713-db50-4780-ba0c-eebf63d4595c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cost-to-Serve Analysis", "children": [{"id": "d092e159-0150-49b1-ad88-89b0d6cf2ebe", "type": "concept", "title": "Activity-based costing for logistics"}, {"id": "84280ed9-0f65-42b5-b714-6ddec1ed2c7c", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer, SKU, order, and channel profitability"}, {"id": "b84f0ffe-8ca0-49f8-bb37-79dbd902a2be", "type": "concept", "title": "Freight audit, invoice matching, and leakage control"}], "description": "Students learn to connect freight cost to customers, products, lanes, and service policies."}]}, {"id": "bfb7b72b-ad04-4624-90f0-23c8e19eab9b", "type": "topic", "title": "Routing, Scheduling and Dispatch Optimization", "description": "Routing and scheduling convert customer promises into feasible transportation plans. Students learn both the logic and constraints behind vehicle movement.", "children": [{"id": "455e2ca2-74b4-479c-9557-e25177ce9899", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Routing Problems", "children": [{"id": "8a2fa151-ed77-490c-95c3-10e97d9e157a", "type": "concept", "title": "Vehicle routing problem, traveling salesperson problem, pickup and delivery, and backhaul matching"}, {"id": "7d396d98-2bdc-4e12-be0c-30c82f1b48de", "type": "concept", "title": "Distance, time windows, capacity, equipment, driver hours, and service constraints"}, {"id": "d237984f-50bd-407b-a877-6b0654eac111", "type": "concept", "title": "Manual planning versus optimization engines"}], "description": "Students learn the practical structure of routing decisions."}, {"id": "66b93daa-8d0e-45a3-ac82-ea030397124d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scheduling and Dispatch", "children": [{"id": "dccaea4f-10c5-41ab-b744-f3fb61edac5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Appointment scheduling, load sequencing, dock times, and dispatch boards"}, {"id": "55f1ade9-c238-4195-a563-aa891b83caae", "type": "concept", "title": "Driver assignment, equipment assignment, and route compliance"}, {"id": "4aa2c836-f4ac-401d-a9ea-0a80c1edd466", "type": "concept", "title": "Exception management, re-routing, and communication protocols"}], "description": "The focus is on execution: turning plans into timed work and responding to exceptions."}, {"id": "943a98cf-f191-4735-80ef-a37dfe6dda3e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Optimization Trade-offs", "children": [{"id": "fe1c6ef9-67fc-4a80-8631-383f71209e30", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, service, reliability, labor, safety, emissions, and customer priority"}, {"id": "3de8cd6d-b109-402c-be0d-6ac1c6b562b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitivity to demand variability and traffic"}, {"id": "70834844-8d7e-4b83-8ca1-2faa803f2bca", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario planning and what-if analysis"}], "description": "Students learn why the mathematically cheapest plan may not be operationally best."}]}, {"id": "8af4fa01-b9f4-47fe-8d81-4bd947dc24b9", "type": "topic", "title": "Distribution Network Design", "description": "A logistics network determines where inventory sits, how orders flow, and how fast customers can be served. This topic builds network design judgment.", "children": [{"id": "d353cf78-64b6-461e-97f1-7ca1fe497a82", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Network Structure", "children": [{"id": "54fe6c72-b9f1-42f7-96a2-6fb21fc0f28c", "type": "concept", "title": "Factories, suppliers, ports, DCs, cross-docks, stores, lockers, and customer nodes"}, {"id": "94c75ebe-5070-47af-9d94-a38fc773c9e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct shipping, hub-and-spoke, pooling, cross-docking, and postponement"}, {"id": "eaec3e22-5acc-485e-a5a9-0a3019aef6fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-echelon and multi-echelon networks"}], "description": "Students learn the design options that shape distribution systems."}, {"id": "2c1b40c1-a70a-4c32-8770-fd7ed1ea535c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Facility Location and Flow", "children": [{"id": "4aa5ec3f-f573-4b5e-aa80-2ea20a107b12", "type": "concept", "title": "Center-of-gravity, network optimization, and lane-flow modeling"}, {"id": "8af86266-b214-4cba-8e1f-b2973754b4d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Inbound, outbound, reverse, and transfer flows"}, {"id": "234a7b8d-fd39-461a-92cd-7b29724e5b04", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity, labor, real estate, tax, risk, and customer-density considerations"}], "description": "The point is to locate facilities and routes around demand, cost, capacity, and service."}, {"id": "e35b8c43-564a-4c48-8bce-ff87ab4a7ffd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Network Strategy", "children": [{"id": "c1a4775d-8af3-483f-866b-ea96f7a987cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Speed versus cost versus resilience"}, {"id": "f2430822-a741-4291-b785-48a7952b10d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Regionalization, nearshoring, and multi-sourcing"}, {"id": "fe45eaa2-4fb1-4d6e-94a5-9cf12ee8259d", "type": "concept", "title": "Network redesign triggers: growth, merger, disruption, service failure, and channel change"}], "description": "Students connect network design to business strategy."}]}, {"id": "3be74a70-643d-4611-99bd-006897d18d02", "type": "topic", "title": "Warehousing, Fulfillment and Inventory Interface", "description": "Transportation and warehousing are tightly linked: shipment size, order timing, storage design, and inventory policy all shape freight performance.", "children": [{"id": "85a07c05-150a-4411-b6fc-e8719875920e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Warehouse Role in Logistics", "children": [{"id": "5249b915-262c-46cd-831d-767a057f1fb7", "type": "concept", "title": "Receiving, putaway, storage, replenishment, picking, packing, shipping, and returns"}, {"id": "500882f6-4717-4007-b596-aca662101bee", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-docking, flow-through, breakbulk, and merge-in-transit"}, {"id": "90d3317b-ff59-44a7-83b2-9232d637505d", "type": "concept", "title": "Warehouse layout, slotting, labor, and dock management"}], "description": "Students learn how facilities support consolidation, postponement, fulfillment, and service."}, {"id": "fca38dea-36ea-47c6-a07c-383a545d82a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory-Service Trade-offs", "children": [{"id": "c81f1a02-a823-4855-8242-d14a4b5cd380", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle stock, safety stock, reorder points, EOQ, and ABC analysis"}, {"id": "2167e445-b98c-4af7-8d3c-5afa2b6b96b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Stockout risk, fill rate, order cycle time, and service levels"}, {"id": "ac4967d1-9cc9-4f88-a34b-fbfca5f17458", "type": "concept", "title": "Pooling, postponement, and inventory placement"}], "description": "The goal is to connect inventory policy to transportation speed and cost."}, {"id": "37dd844b-eb83-4bfd-bc74-21fc79bf954d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fulfillment Execution", "children": [{"id": "4be6a80b-30f8-400e-ab90-ec0d7829e37d", "type": "concept", "title": "Order batching, wave planning, picking methods, packing, labeling, and compliance"}, {"id": "cd835d4a-09d9-49db-a46f-26f02b114bd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Parcel, LTL, truckload, and customer pickup handoff"}, {"id": "ce044b97-7096-4c0f-b017-761679378017", "type": "concept", "title": "WMS, barcode, RFID, automation, and labor standards"}], "description": "Students learn the operational details behind customer-ready shipments."}]}, {"id": "479cdbd8-3b5e-4168-b4e7-c8662b11a207", "type": "topic", "title": "Demand Planning, S&OP and Capacity Alignment", "description": "Logistics cannot perform well when demand, inventory, and capacity plans are disconnected. This section links transportation decisions to planning cadence.", "children": [{"id": "cadbf517-f3a1-49e9-a210-b57815ca2acc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand Signals and Forecasts", "children": [{"id": "cefc0c3c-0ae2-4a69-abca-4a10b77de5d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand patterns, seasonality, promotions, launches, and forecast error"}, {"id": "ea77ad9f-0bf6-4d23-b1f3-285bd3e4d0cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Moving averages, exponential smoothing, causal forecasts, and judgment overlays"}, {"id": "2ba6028e-ce2b-4ac6-b50b-af0c6a3e22c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Forecast bias, accuracy, and exception review"}], "description": "Students learn what logistics planners need from demand planning."}, {"id": "17b9b079-1f94-4fb0-9194-85e0d2271d62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "S&OP and Logistics Capacity", "children": [{"id": "14e0c107-9347-40a3-ae86-53583719a62b", "type": "concept", "title": "Sales and operations planning cadence"}, {"id": "0fbcb30a-2349-4d02-a831-491690d3a5a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity planning for carriers, warehouses, ports, and labor"}, {"id": "71363be5-5b3d-4a53-93d7-8724b88e5a80", "type": "concept", "title": "Peak planning, constraint review, and contingency capacity"}], "description": "The purpose is to align freight capacity, warehouse labor, and inventory with expected demand."}, {"id": "fed4de7b-1d9f-471e-863d-983468564851", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integrated Planning Decisions", "children": [{"id": "26480dd3-97b8-4cef-b3e6-696c3af41a97", "type": "concept", "title": "Order frequency, minimum order quantities, replenishment cadence, and shipment consolidation"}, {"id": "cb4c1abc-fa7e-4d3a-9e09-13ce6476d323", "type": "concept", "title": "Expedite prevention and service policy design"}, {"id": "518e41c9-ebfd-4e5b-ac1d-115cf4f28650", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade-offs among forecast accuracy, buffer inventory, and transport flexibility"}], "description": "Students see how planning choices create logistics consequences."}]}, {"id": "1531c922-6ad0-4867-866f-a61f02cefad9", "type": "topic", "title": "Last-Mile, Ecommerce and Omnichannel Logistics", "description": "The last mile is often the most visible and expensive part of logistics. This topic focuses on customer promise, density, delivery options, and returns.", "children": [{"id": "2646c3b1-6dbe-4f9a-b98a-3e40578d1f97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Last-Mile Models", "children": [{"id": "78415b7e-5ee7-49f3-bda5-7e6efd318231", "type": "concept", "title": "Parcel networks, local courier, gig delivery, store fulfillment, lockers, pickup points, and white-glove service"}, {"id": "0d87b202-8415-4814-9bd8-c8859a1199ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Same-day, next-day, scheduled, and economy delivery options"}, {"id": "e457f9b1-1d9e-446f-b7bf-4b67dd70cc05", "type": "concept", "title": "Urban, suburban, and rural delivery economics"}], "description": "Students compare the delivery structures used in ecommerce and retail."}, {"id": "5f82851f-c6ef-4ef6-9905-6cd4ca470b1c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Customer Promise Design", "children": [{"id": "f3c18350-cd03-480d-824b-0f370ce20a90", "type": "concept", "title": "Delivery speed, accuracy, visibility, installation, returns, and communication"}, {"id": "825806d3-50c7-46b1-b110-23db1e81b406", "type": "concept", "title": "Free shipping thresholds, delivery fees, and service tiers"}, {"id": "13ccfb0c-4d69-4bfa-83a8-ed84146fd26e", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer experience metrics and failure recovery"}], "description": "The point is to design delivery promises that are attractive and operationally possible."}, {"id": "e8ec6480-369e-4c29-ba85-3f06bc71b975", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Returns and Reverse Flow", "children": [{"id": "0ecd41cd-548d-4c57-b445-8f0ee98ea58a", "type": "concept", "title": "Return authorization, inspection, disposition, refurbish, recycle, and resale"}, {"id": "ffe787ac-1759-444d-8c62-07249e963ff2", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost of returns and fraud control"}, {"id": "2fda9519-4deb-4702-8760-72ebe43a509d", "type": "concept", "title": "Reverse logistics network design and customer satisfaction"}], "description": "Students learn why returns are a strategic logistics process, not an afterthought."}]}, {"id": "9763ab87-a725-4497-bca2-9d634059907e", "type": "topic", "title": "International Logistics, Ports and Global Freight", "description": "Global logistics adds distance, time, uncertainty, regulation, and multi-party coordination. This unit introduces the operating logic of international freight.", "children": [{"id": "7916d05c-ddc3-410c-a535-d2cb0924d70c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global Freight Modes", "children": [{"id": "b9c7c6fb-4ffc-465e-a067-0307975cab71", "type": "concept", "title": "Containerization, vessels, ports, terminals, air cargo, rail corridors, and drayage"}, {"id": "4a200c09-1838-4140-8e43-910567cf0b07", "type": "concept", "title": "Transit time, cutoffs, sailings, dwell time, and port congestion"}, {"id": "57020432-36b5-49b1-833a-eedb5f187f70", "type": "concept", "title": "Freight forwarders, NVOCCs, brokers, and customs intermediaries"}], "description": "Students learn how ocean, air, rail, truck, and intermodal systems connect across borders."}, {"id": "e18aaef7-2871-443b-a028-9c04dab4f353", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Incoterms and Responsibilities", "children": [{"id": "86abd1d3-784c-442d-83d2-e06052b832be", "type": "concept", "title": "EXW, FCA, FOB, CFR, CIF, CPT, CIP, DAP, DPU, and DDP"}, {"id": "dacb274f-0b2a-4b59-b099-7d541c8ffcb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Transfer of risk, freight payment, insurance, and documentation responsibility"}, {"id": "38597835-dfd3-42aa-a20f-f58385b2267e", "type": "concept", "title": "Common incoterms mistakes and landed cost implications"}], "description": "The goal is to understand how commercial terms assign cost, risk, and responsibility."}, {"id": "a574abc0-6456-4bf9-aec6-d424ed851415", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global Risk and Coordination", "children": [{"id": "17695b3a-858d-4d0d-aaf7-b7ced4afc68c", "type": "concept", "title": "Geopolitical risk, port disruption, weather, labor actions, piracy, and sanctions"}, {"id": "c287f4ab-2466-479b-8796-ebac03b5101d", "type": "concept", "title": "Buffer time, alternate gateways, dual routing, and supplier coordination"}, {"id": "0e7841a6-e753-46e1-81bd-b82d11f74848", "type": "concept", "title": "Visibility, milestones, and exception management"}], "description": "Students learn how global logistics plans deal with uncertainty."}]}, {"id": "a308ad5d-bacf-447b-a07e-3e40121517db", "type": "topic", "title": "Customs, Trade Compliance and Security", "description": "Trade compliance protects the firm from delays, penalties, seizures, and reputational harm. Students learn the core compliance processes logistics managers must understand.", "children": [{"id": "25b50fd4-f5a0-4dee-8290-a692f91bc827", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Customs Documentation", "children": [{"id": "4d0f833b-2e12-40d2-8c97-c21cc37c5ee2", "type": "concept", "title": "Commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, airway bill, certificate of origin, and entry documents"}, {"id": "459a6b0a-42a1-40c6-a713-b9637b29d239", "type": "concept", "title": "HS classification, valuation, country of origin, and duty calculation"}, {"id": "1bb3a246-e27c-4b10-8187-c34b3de9fb8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Recordkeeping, audit trail, and broker coordination"}], "description": "Students learn the paperwork and data needed for legal cross-border movement."}, {"id": "abac3473-6c10-4d12-bf08-5cc3e1cdc459", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regulatory Compliance", "children": [{"id": "af37fddb-6b49-46f7-81fd-9ee5b5efa4f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Import/export controls, denied parties, sanctions, anti-dumping, and product regulations"}, {"id": "f98c82e3-7b73-46e1-9493-55f94f6c7cfa", "type": "concept", "title": "C-TPAT, bonded warehouses, free trade zones, and trusted trader programs"}, {"id": "b77a5aaa-6557-464a-b319-9944dabb8659", "type": "concept", "title": "Compliance ownership and escalation"}], "description": "The point is to connect logistics decisions to trade rules and government controls."}, {"id": "433fb844-4f94-4615-a939-9fe40cb32a02", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cargo Security and Risk", "children": [{"id": "20533039-8ab5-4463-9349-762d36b4ee30", "type": "concept", "title": "Chain of custody, seals, inspections, screening, and cargo theft prevention"}, {"id": "e47f0651-e596-4916-b8db-e5898af89c2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cybersecurity for logistics data and systems"}, {"id": "a94fce15-213b-4dc4-a4b6-af7d0729499d", "type": "concept", "title": "Insurance, claims, and incident response"}], "description": "Students learn how security requirements shape logistics execution."}]}, {"id": "5956e700-90f1-4df8-8a1b-c70f3307ecfc", "type": "topic", "title": "Intermodal, Multimodal and Infrastructure Systems", "description": "Modern logistics depends on infrastructure and handoffs across modes. This topic focuses on nodes, transfers, bottlenecks, and infrastructure capacity.", "children": [{"id": "464f0b9f-2224-4b9d-8c6b-5b547043e8c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intermodal Systems", "children": [{"id": "7c0e94b5-817c-4c85-88f4-123a8bc5e04c", "type": "concept", "title": "Drayage, ramps, terminals, chassis, containers, and rail intermodal"}, {"id": "f12c2fba-539f-43a6-bfd1-6371a1538320", "type": "concept", "title": "Ramp selection, cutoffs, dwell, detention, demurrage, and equipment availability"}, {"id": "456b2088-702e-4758-8f93-bb6c0ba8cd1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Intermodal cost, emissions, service, and reliability trade-offs"}], "description": "Students learn how containers and trailers move across truck, rail, ocean, and inland hubs."}, {"id": "3c567e4b-5728-46cc-8ecd-9aa709dd033f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Infrastructure and Bottlenecks", "children": [{"id": "87c5bbaa-ca74-4ad6-8895-86ae11a0db09", "type": "concept", "title": "Capacity, congestion, maintenance, weather exposure, and labor availability"}, {"id": "c1528782-cdb2-44ad-be7e-c8825b92add3", "type": "concept", "title": "Port and terminal operations"}, {"id": "b277d586-b042-4740-8f97-8cc9e874ef70", "type": "concept", "title": "Public policy, infrastructure investment, and freight corridors"}], "description": "The focus is on how ports, roads, bridges, rail, airports, and warehouses constrain logistics performance."}, {"id": "eb57ccbb-72d0-400d-93ad-e0cb9a7ba6a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multimodal Coordination", "children": [{"id": "0780ab7a-285b-40cc-8b24-6ffbdedc6538", "type": "concept", "title": "Handoff milestones, documentation, visibility, and exception ownership"}, {"id": "34fceda4-8a10-42ec-bff4-21b63db901e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Through bills, freight forwarding, and integrated service providers"}, {"id": "b11853ed-3077-454c-b642-98beb6b54575", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk at interfaces and buffers between modes"}], "description": "Students learn how to manage movement when no single party controls the whole journey."}]}, {"id": "083b9dbc-21fe-4840-9559-224edc885408", "type": "topic", "title": "Logistics Technology, TMS, WMS and Visibility", "description": "Technology lets logistics teams plan, execute, monitor, and improve flow. This unit explains the systems landscape and how data becomes operational visibility.", "children": [{"id": "c63df780-71e6-4aed-ab18-9a7a4583c870", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transportation Management Systems", "children": [{"id": "e8f8f90f-a697-4692-8204-17204489aedd", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning, rating, tendering, tracking, freight audit, settlement, and reporting"}, {"id": "7fab82f2-1f9a-48b3-9b89-905b42322d77", "type": "concept", "title": "Carrier portals, EDI/API connectivity, and load boards"}, {"id": "7ccdf2cf-9f9f-4363-a871-270b3cd2442c", "type": "concept", "title": "Optimization, dynamic pricing, and exception workflows"}], "description": "Students learn what TMS platforms do and why they matter."}, {"id": "46fcdf62-3c4a-446b-a429-2d18a1d386ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Warehouse and Yard Systems", "children": [{"id": "c427d030-e000-4790-969e-d405f3fbfc03", "type": "concept", "title": "WMS, YMS, labor management, slotting, scanning, RFID, and automation"}, {"id": "a2450f82-cc23-4b52-9f0c-b2c70de4d3da", "type": "concept", "title": "Appointment scheduling, dock visibility, and trailer tracking"}, {"id": "43b8039f-ddba-4e54-bf75-60b022fe8f5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Integration among ERP, OMS, WMS, TMS, and carrier systems"}], "description": "The point is to understand how warehouse and yard execution systems connect to transport."}, {"id": "1aa520ae-0c78-4448-8fab-6bdd5e527500", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visibility and Control Towers", "children": [{"id": "8cbc4903-4f97-4806-9eb3-7497aa1b7eb3", "type": "concept", "title": "GPS, telematics, IoT sensors, ELDs, AIS, APIs, milestones, and event data"}, {"id": "0228e23a-d191-4ac4-b7cf-192a854e4780", "type": "concept", "title": "Predictive ETA, alerts, exception triage, and customer communication"}, {"id": "5acbba32-93e8-43fa-af94-825131580b70", "type": "concept", "title": "Data quality, master data, and governance"}], "description": "Students learn how real-time logistics data supports decision making."}]}, {"id": "fb514a10-fe2e-430f-80ad-cbb2e442b451", "type": "topic", "title": "Logistics Analytics, KPIs and Decision Support", "description": "World-class logistics managers use data to diagnose performance, evaluate trade-offs, and improve decisions. This section builds practical analytics fluency.", "children": [{"id": "37f6d923-184e-45b6-884b-735a9cc10dc9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Logistics KPI Design", "children": [{"id": "a1c68186-2b0a-4961-ba44-7821379fd4a7", "type": "concept", "title": "On-time pickup, on-time delivery, tender acceptance, cost per mile, cost per order, claims, damage, dwell, and utilization"}, {"id": "5101b803-f5d8-4121-af01-adf7ab602af1", "type": "concept", "title": "Service, cost, productivity, quality, sustainability, and resilience metrics"}, {"id": "40eec463-0fa5-4afa-8b37-7dbd232755ca", "type": "concept", "title": "KPI definitions, targets, ownership, and review cadence"}], "description": "Students learn which measures matter and how to avoid metric overload."}, {"id": "7c3ccf72-c87c-461e-9104-ab1d5d1271b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Decision Analytics", "children": [{"id": "ead6b676-f486-4a65-a2e5-057cf5412686", "type": "concept", "title": "Lane analysis, shipment consolidation, mode choice, routing, and facility scenarios"}, {"id": "f0bb57df-ec58-4e5e-b742-44cc89729e65", "type": "concept", "title": "Regression, clustering, simulation, optimization, and dashboarding basics"}, {"id": "44259d9a-909d-42ac-8ba1-e6fd8975374b", "type": "concept", "title": "Data visualization and executive decision briefs"}], "description": "The goal is to model logistics choices using clear assumptions and sensitivity."}, {"id": "ea1d47c0-0c42-4265-93e1-ae1d43e3e061", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Performance Improvement", "children": [{"id": "fd9451a5-66dc-4b22-bd07-af3cc34fe3b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Root-cause analysis, Pareto analysis, control charts, and variance review"}, {"id": "88951349-c243-41aa-aeb4-3c24897fa135", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuous improvement projects and benefits tracking"}, {"id": "5299e796-d7bf-42de-9d81-7ba765dec970", "type": "concept", "title": "Benchmarking against internal history and external data"}], "description": "Students learn to turn metrics into action."}]}, {"id": "96a426f3-a2d5-4921-ae5f-defcfcbe54e1", "type": "topic", "title": "Risk, Resilience and Disruption Response", "description": "Logistics networks operate under disruption. This topic teaches students to map risk, prepare contingencies, and recover service.", "children": [{"id": "5ffff245-5218-4e33-b4dc-e07b8ff44114", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Risk Identification", "children": [{"id": "c9be27fa-0b9d-463c-8faa-30967af145e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier, carrier, lane, port, facility, weather, cyber, labor, geopolitical, and demand risks"}, {"id": "33b7ef82-8db3-40d0-9057-73b5909a1332", "type": "concept", "title": "Single points of failure and critical nodes"}, {"id": "70d541bf-0911-437e-bde7-a12965768ecf", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk probability, impact, detectability, and velocity"}], "description": "Students learn to recognize vulnerabilities before they become crises."}, {"id": "b19a50b6-ab7b-4a78-8ffc-02652eaaf7a3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resilience Design", "children": [{"id": "99210d28-14ec-4f64-83cc-8fa7e2511ed2", "type": "concept", "title": "Redundant carriers, alternate ports, safety capacity, inventory buffers, and flexible routing"}, {"id": "8ef84776-68b4-4b99-8361-22ab06da036c", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario planning, playbooks, and business continuity planning"}, {"id": "78e57d5e-9dd5-4a0e-8040-9d29cc1796fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade-offs among efficiency, resilience, and working capital"}], "description": "The point is to build optionality without making the network unaffordable."}, {"id": "de59c4b0-3e58-4d96-a0d5-3ce746050eda", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Disruption Response", "children": [{"id": "790759ef-6ae0-4d17-b06d-ca1cac4a4555", "type": "concept", "title": "War rooms, escalation, decision rights, communications, and recovery priorities"}, {"id": "e9a4d297-e900-4a7b-91aa-5ffd4c627ff8", "type": "concept", "title": "Expediting, allocation, substitution, and customer segmentation during disruption"}, {"id": "56ee1fe4-a7e4-4900-9b80-33693cea9f05", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-event learning and resilience investment cases"}], "description": "Students learn the operating discipline of crisis logistics."}]}, {"id": "ddcc295a-6538-44da-8cf8-99f443ac7be2", "type": "topic", "title": "Sustainable and Responsible Logistics", "description": "Logistics choices affect emissions, communities, labor, safety, and waste. This section makes sustainability an operational design problem.", "children": [{"id": "bc1a7a4e-99f8-45c0-bc91-7b00be61c46e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Emissions and Energy", "children": [{"id": "dd0701dc-e368-4dc6-a537-593bb7b96a3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope 1, Scope 2, and Scope 3 logistics emissions"}, {"id": "fa4e2ce1-7764-44fc-987d-b3babd8134a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Mode shift, route optimization, load factor, alternative fuels, EVs, and renewable energy"}, {"id": "34891231-709f-4e2e-b32f-4858d8431f15", "type": "concept", "title": "Carbon accounting, emissions factors, and customer reporting"}], "description": "Students learn where logistics emissions come from and how to reduce them."}, {"id": "7bfc2211-78b7-4478-8116-6b6c2a4a3159", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Circular and Reverse Logistics", "children": [{"id": "62667990-5896-4047-9213-5bc60696c04d", "type": "concept", "title": "Returns, repair, refurbishment, remanufacturing, recycling, and disposal"}, {"id": "457f4b5c-0b23-42be-9273-0589e4014d1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Packaging reduction, reusable packaging, and closed-loop systems"}, {"id": "87993a00-26fd-405c-95b3-50a28be820d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Product design and logistics design for circularity"}], "description": "The focus is on recovering value and reducing waste."}, {"id": "64787e5a-cd29-4327-9f04-aaffcad558ce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social Responsibility", "children": [{"id": "9848f928-e98e-42fa-a3c6-062f1463a4e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Driver safety, labor practices, warehouse ergonomics, and fair scheduling"}, {"id": "d1aa1e8c-c99e-4e6c-810b-0362e19f5ff6", "type": "concept", "title": "Community impacts of freight, congestion, noise, and air quality"}, {"id": "c4cb41a0-9ead-458e-9468-9283ecd95a3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical sourcing, transparency, and supplier/carrier standards"}], "description": "Students learn that responsible logistics includes people and communities."}]}, {"id": "4f8d0c5f-c3b0-4413-b6af-32dfdd987fbf", "type": "topic", "title": "Regulation, Safety and Legal Environment", "description": "Transportation operates in a regulated environment. Students learn the rules and responsibilities that shape safe, lawful logistics execution.", "children": [{"id": "6fde868b-b4f8-4124-a3f7-f9d14e6fbd7a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transportation Regulation", "children": [{"id": "b97fbfd6-e96b-41fd-9176-a5243c7e990f", "type": "concept", "title": "Motor carrier authority, hours of service, ELDs, hazardous materials, and safety ratings"}, {"id": "54c23b8f-9613-42b0-a16e-c164fccfd969", "type": "concept", "title": "Rail, ocean, air, and parcel regulatory context"}, {"id": "76298ab3-17ed-4812-a61c-b86c87c639d3", "type": "concept", "title": "FMCSA, DOT, FMC, FAA, TSA, and international bodies"}], "description": "Students learn the regulatory basics that differ by mode and jurisdiction."}, {"id": "fbe05152-227d-429e-97b2-fa949c9ca480", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Safety Management", "children": [{"id": "7adda5bf-5534-45b3-a253-ad813fe1f18a", "type": "concept", "title": "Driver safety, warehouse safety, loading securement, hazmat handling, and incident reporting"}, {"id": "4dc7f6dc-2247-4406-bbaa-3d596186f548", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety KPIs, audits, training, and corrective actions"}, {"id": "29c1f42e-05f0-403c-a8ff-c54c10ce4e32", "type": "concept", "title": "Insurance, liability, claims, and risk transfer"}], "description": "The goal is to make safety a managed system, not a slogan."}, {"id": "969bb369-8b4d-4b35-b0fb-4b6b7f39557c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Legal and Ethical Issues", "children": [{"id": "7d741b3e-600c-4729-a757-0b44aad59bda", "type": "concept", "title": "Contracts, fraud, cargo theft, bribery, sanctions, antitrust, and confidentiality"}, {"id": "cf400d92-4514-4568-88ff-3490c9dff54f", "type": "concept", "title": "Data privacy and cybersecurity in logistics platforms"}, {"id": "d8e6ac3c-91ff-4e98-8dd6-f797fce85cdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical decision making under service and cost pressure"}], "description": "Students learn common legal and ethical pitfalls in logistics."}]}, {"id": "ad8c3115-23e2-4470-a89a-de1a9852b783", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone Transportation Case and Network Recommendation", "description": "The course culminates in a professional logistics decision case. Students diagnose a network, model alternatives, and recommend an executable transportation plan.", "children": [{"id": "d0f9096c-bf97-4b5b-9791-29bd442880b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case Diagnosis", "children": [{"id": "72d21274-9d67-45e7-81be-477a5ab57dd2", "type": "concept", "title": "Current network, lanes, modes, volumes, costs, service failures, and constraints"}, {"id": "23225530-ddd4-44de-ba18-fad018b7f9ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholders, customer promise, inventory impact, and risk exposure"}, {"id": "07c6d046-4df6-4816-8a10-4fa10c3ab298", "type": "concept", "title": "Data gaps, assumptions, and decision criteria"}], "description": "Students begin by defining the logistics problem and its business stakes."}, {"id": "d1d090ba-bb2a-4426-9653-f9efbaf8c966", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Alternative Design", "children": [{"id": "0476591b-923c-4b26-864f-2725c528aafb", "type": "concept", "title": "Mode mix, carrier strategy, routing, facility use, last-mile design, and technology support"}, {"id": "c64386cc-f1f6-465a-bcf1-f62de6969535", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, service, emissions, resilience, and implementation trade-offs"}, {"id": "eb8782c3-9822-478b-8c2a-15cf237f7ff8", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitivity analysis and scenario planning"}], "description": "The capstone requires students to create and compare feasible logistics options."}, {"id": "ff97c125-948a-42cd-8d97-de98c61558fe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Executive Recommendation", "children": [{"id": "57d5b704-16cd-4b6e-b292-7b6a9f45c209", "type": "concept", "title": "Recommendation memo, dashboard, network map, and implementation roadmap"}, {"id": "69554be6-8c78-4287-b621-665fd951e981", "type": "concept", "title": "Carrier, warehouse, systems, compliance, and change-management actions"}, {"id": "323789a3-2572-43ba-abed-a73246c7be9a", "type": "concept", "title": "KPIs, control plan, and post-implementation review"}], "description": "Students finish by presenting a decision-ready logistics plan."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$ltmjson$::jsonb,
